# Task 2: Broadcast TFs

```
Create a node that broadcasts the following TFs:
baselink→arucomarkerapproachframe;
baselink→arucomarkertargetframe;
Where thearucomarkerapproachframeandarucomarkertargetframe
are the frames of the Aruco marker with respect to the base link.
```
```
The ”approach” frame is the original aruco marker frame with an offset
along the z-axis (e.g. 0.5 meters).
```
```
You can modify the ”2arucotfbroadcaster.py” file in the ”lab3” pkg.
You need to get the transformation from thebaselinkto theheadfrontcamerargbopticalframe,
since the Aruco marker is attached to the head of the robot (check the
tf tree).
```
```
Therfore you need to concatenate the transformations (use PyKDL):
baselink→headfrontcamerargbopticalframe
headfrontcamerargbopticalframe→arucomarkertargetframe.
arucomarkertargetframe→arucomarkerapproachframe.
```

