# Grasping in simulation is complex... →LinkAttacher

```
Being able to successfully grasp an object in simulation is a complex task
requiring specific tuning of the simulation friction parameters.
```
```
The following repository contains 2 different ROS2 packages, which en-
able the attachment of 2 different entity links in Gazebo. This attach-
ment is done through a simple ROS2/Gazebo plugin.
```
```
This plugin is useful for forcely grasping an object in simulation without
the need to tune the simulation parameters.
```
```
You are encouraged to try grasping with/without the plugin!
```
```
LinkAttacherinstall
```
```
Inside thesrcfolder of your ROS2 workspace (tiagows), clone the repos-
itory and build its packages:
git clone https://github.com/IFRA-Cranfield/IFRA_LinkAttacher
cd ..
colcon build --packages-select linkattacher_msgs
ros2_linkattacher
```

# LinkAttacher: Activate the plugin

```
The tiago simulation automatically loads a gazebo ”world” file at startup.
This file path is:
pal_gazebo_worlds/worlds/eut_kitchen.world
```
```
To activate the plugin, we need to add the following line at the end of
the mentioned world file (just before the closing tag¡/world¿):
```
```
<plugin name = "gazebo_link_attacher" filename =
"libgazebo_link_attacher.so"/>
```

